.el .ds Aq '
.TH SPT-STATUS 1  "status " 
.SH NAME
status \- Read\-only status API controls
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstatus\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read\-only status API controls
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
status\-serve(1)
Run the status API server in foreground (rare — supervisor normally hosts inline when `[status_api].enabled = true`)
.TP
status\-status(1)
Show whether the API is bound + how to reach it
.TP
status\-token(1)
Bearer\-token management for the status API auth
.TP
status\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  spt status status
  spt status status \-\-output json
  spt status serve \-\-config /etc/spt/spt.toml
  spt status token rotate
